    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "Perfect! \u2705 The fix is confirmed to work. Both `FRAI-SPEC.md` and `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml` are now created when running `frai gate init --ci`.\n\n**Summary of the fix:**\n\nThe bug was in how the `gate` command passed arguments to the `frai-gate` subprocess. The issue was:\n\n- The parent `frai` program has a `--ci` option defined globally (line 605)\n- When running `frai gate init --ci`, commander was consuming the `--ci` flag at the parent level before it could reach the `gate` subcommand\n- The `args` array passed to the subprocess action didn't include `--ci`\n\n**The solution:**\nChanged from capturing parsed `args` from commander to directly extracting all arguments from `process.argv` after the `gate` keyword. This bypasses commander's option parsing and passes all flags through unchanged to the `frai-gate` subprocess:\n\n```typescript\nconst gateIndex = process.argv.indexOf('gate');\nconst gateArgs = process.argv.slice(gateIndex + 1);\n```\n\nThe fix has been built and tested successfully. The `--ci` flag is now properly passed through to `frai-gate`.",
